# Still more guild chat (kind guild): what regulars say to each other in /gu between everything else.
# Hellos and "not long left for me" (real logons and logoffs are kind session, said by the schedule; these
# lines are said by a bot that stays on), ribbing, real-life small talk, vague guild plans, crafting asks and
# offers, small wins and losses, inside jokes, and asking how everyone is. Any realm, no place names.
# Real-life lines invite the player_rl_<subject> replies ("ugh, work", "gl on the test") so a guildmate
# answers in kind. Lines never promise an invite, an event or what a guildmate will do. New writing
# (see docs/bot-voices).

# ---------------- Hellos and checking in ----------------
@kind guild
@topic social
@who *
@invites ask_howareyou
[hey|hi|hiya|heya] [guild|guildies|folks], [hows everyone doing|how is everybody|hows it going]?
